class:: BlipPeak
summary:: Positive Fejér pulse with optional DC removal
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/BlipExtensions, Classes/BlipAD, Classes/BlipDecay, Classes/BlipDiff, Classes/BlipDisp, Classes/BlipFB, Classes/BlipFrac, Classes/BlipInt, Classes/BlipKernel, Classes/BlipPM, Classes/BlipPower, Classes/BlipSeries, Classes/BlipWidth

description::

BlipPeak squares a normalized finite sinc ratio to produce a nonnegative
Fejér pulse with peak one. code::center:: continuously subtracts its known DC
component and renormalizes the aligned peak.

The phase-wrap limit is evaluated analytically, not by clamping a small
denominator. Harmonics stop at the Nyquist-limited count, and topology changes
fade over one block. Centered mode is no longer nonnegative because DC removal
creates a small negative floor.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/Blip::. Both create compact finite
harmonic pulses, but BlipPeak uses triangular spectral magnitudes including a
known DC term and is nonnegative before centering.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Frequency in Hz. Audio or control rate; signed values are valid.

argument:: numharm
Highest requested harmonic, sampled once per block and clipped to
code::1..2048:: before limiting.

argument:: center
Audio- or control-rate interpolation from the raw positive pulse at zero to
the zero-mean form at one. Values are clipped to code::0..1::.

argument:: mul
Post-processing multiplier.

argument:: add
Post-processing offset.

examples::

code::
(
{ BlipPeak.ar(12, 80, mul: 0.2) }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{ BlipPeak.ar(100, 30, 1, 0.1) }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{ Ringz.ar(BlipPeak.ar(4, 80), 1200, 0.1) * 0.1 }.play;
)
::

code::
// Modulating all parameters for a dynamic sound
(
{ BlipPeak.ar(SinOsc.kr(0.2).exprange(50, 400), MouseY.kr(1, 100), LFNoise1.kr(0.5).range(0, 1)) ! 2 * 0.1 }.play;
)
::
